# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Novus Jobs — server configuration
#
# Copy this file to `server/.env` and edit. Every value here has a default:
# the app starts and runs with an empty file. What you set here is the stuff
# that cannot live in the database — credentials, ports, paths.
#
# Everything about YOU — your stack, your English level, where you live, which
# platforms are on and how often they run — is configured in the app itself and
# stored in the database, so changing it never needs a restart.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where the dashboard listens. Bound to 127.0.0.1 and not configurable: this is
# your CV and your job hunt, and it has no authentication because it is not
# meant to be reachable from outside your machine.
# PORT=47831

# Where the database, the logs and your CV live. Defaults to `server/data`.
# Point it outside the repo if you want your data to survive a fresh clone.
# DATA_DIR=/Users/you/.novus-jobs/data

# Default time slots (0-23, local time) for platforms that run on a schedule.
# Each platform can override this from the Integrations screen.
# SCHEDULE_HOURS=9,13,18

# Set to false to never run searches automatically. The manual button still
# works. Useful while you are setting things up.
# SCHEDULER_ENABLED=true

# Which platforms start enabled the FIRST time the app runs. After that the
# on/off switch in Integrations wins and this value is ignored.
# JOB_SOURCES=linkedin,getonbrd

# Where browser sessions are stored. Outside the repo on purpose: it is the one
# thing here you cannot regenerate, so no build or clean should touch it.
# BROWSER_PROFILES_DIR=/Users/you/.novus-jobs/browser-profiles

# Set to false to watch the scraper work in a visible window. For debugging.
# BROWSER_HEADLESS=true

# ── The LLM judge (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A second pair of eyes over the rules: it can reject what the rules let in and
# overturn what the rules rejected for reasons it reads better. Without a key,
# the rules decide alone and everything still works.
# It also powers the optional "read my CV with the model" button during setup —
# which is the only thing in this project that sends your data anywhere, and
# only when you click it. See docs/PRIVACY.md.
# Free tier: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# JUDGE_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash

# ── Email notifications (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# All three are required for mail to work; with any of them missing, nothing is
# sent and the dashboard is the only channel. https://resend.com
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# MAIL_FROM=novus-jobs@yourdomain.com
# MAIL_TO=you@example.com

# The URL used in those emails to link back to the dashboard.
# DASHBOARD_URL=http://127.0.0.1:47831/

# ── Applying ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The account the "apply by email" button opens Gmail with. A credential, not a
# preference, which is why it lives here and not in the app.
# GMAIL_ACCOUNT=you@gmail.com
